# Parrot recording v2
# GENERATED by generate.py. Do not edit. Change the generator and rerun it.
#
# Replay overhead benchmark, measured phase: 5 presses of the Shift_L key per
# second.
#
# 300 presses, one every 200 ms, for 60 s. Each press is a keydown and a keyup
# 12 ms later, about as long as a key is held in the recordings. Key events
# are most of what the recordings replay, and with the xdotool injector every
# one of them is a process that also sleeps 12 ms after its event, so a press
# costs two process starts and 24 ms of sleep that the recording does not
# have.
#
# Shift_L is a modifier. The xtest injector sends it the way xdotool does, the
# first keycode of its modifier and then the key itself, which here is the
# same keycode. xlogo binds no modifier combination, and the screenshot checks
# phase that runs after this one would fail if it changed anything.
#
# The wait comes FIRST inside the loop body. `loop` clears the pending wait
# when it jumps, so a wait written just before the `loop` line would be
# dropped on every iteration but the last.

startcommand = xlogo
windowtitle = xlogo
windowclass = xlogo

log Shift presses 5 Hz: 300 presses of the Shift_L key, one every 200 ms, held 12 ms, for 60 s
label press
wait 0.188000
keydown Shift_L
wait 0.012000
keyup Shift_L
loop press 300
log Shift presses 5 Hz complete: 300 presses in 60 s of recorded time
